WEBVTT

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:04.640
"Shusei Tokuda"

00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:03.940
Is he...?

00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:09.400
"Chuya Nakahara"

00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:08.730
Just watch.

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:14.150
"Osamu Dazai"

00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:14.980
Dear Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> ,

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:20.530
I don't think I can handle living
in this prison of books.

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:22.900
Thus, I have decided to run.

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:24.730
Immediately!

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:31.480
Um, Chuya- <i>san</i> .

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:34.940
I keep climbing and not getting anywhere.

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:37.360
Is there even an exit?

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:39.530
Of course not.

00:02:41.110 --> 00:02:43.280
You said there was!

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:44.900
I did!

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:46.400
And I lied!

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:48.730
Why did you lie?

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:50.860
'Cause it's fun!

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:54.360
Nakahara- <i>kun</i> , that's not appropriate behavior.

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:59.150
I can't take it anymore.
I'll just jump off the ledge and die!

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:01.820
Oh, yeah? Have fun!

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:04.230
Dazai- <i>kun</i> , calm down.

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:05.480
Correct.

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:08.690
"Toson Shimazaki"

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:10.030
If you want to die, inform me in writing.

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:14.360
Shimazaki, you can't expect that
from this peach flower boy.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:16.480
He's not even serious.

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:17.690
He's not?

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:20.150
He's tried a bunch of times.

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:22.440
With women, too.

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:24.320
It's mean to say it like that!

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:25.730
It's true, though.

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:27.980
How many lovers' suicides have you screwed up?

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:31.360
I just happened to survive, that's all.

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:34.400
Dazai- <i>kun</i> , just come down.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:36.940
Let's talk about this.

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:39.690
If you want to get him down,
this is the fast way.

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:48.530
I'm dead!

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:50.900
It hurts so much I'm dead!
I'm dead from the pain!

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:54.570
That's hilarious!

00:03:54.570 --> 00:03:57.190
You're a lively one, huh?

00:03:57.190 --> 00:04:00.400
You're nothing but a soul. How could you die?

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:03.280
How do we know unless I try?

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:07.900
"Episode 2"

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:10.820
Sorry, sorry.

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:12.940
Forgive me. I didn't mean any harm.

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:14.860
You meant nothing but harm.

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:17.900
Nakahara- <i>kun</i> , why do you tell lies like that?

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:19.780
Because I'm bored.

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:23.070
Unless you're delving,
there's nothing to do here.

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:26.730
Is there really no exit?

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:28.280
No idea.

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:30.280
Because...

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:33.110
Dear Kenji Miyazawa- <i>sensei</i> ,

00:04:33.110 --> 00:04:35.280
I can't take this anymore!

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:39.900
There's nothing to drink here,
and I can't take it anymore!

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:43.280
I'm leaving! I'm getting out of here!

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:48.030
I gave up on leaving by the stairs...

00:04:52.780 --> 00:04:55.440
Fell and broke my butt. The end.

00:04:56.650 --> 00:04:59.570
So you fell too, Chuya?

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:04.780
Yeah. You and I are broken-butt buddies,
peach flower boy.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:07.440
I've been wondering...

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:10.860
What's a "peach flower boy"?

00:05:10.860 --> 00:05:14.280
He looks like that, but actually
he loves peach flowers!

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:16.400
What's my face got to do with it?

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:17.320
Oh, I see.

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:19.730
It's got something to do with his life
before he came here?

00:05:19.730 --> 00:05:22.440
Just like me and Shusei.

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:25.900
I can't believe you looked at that ceiling
and decided to climb up there.

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:28.280
There're many rooms here.

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:30.360
But none of them lead to the outside.

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:36.190
So it's normal to assume that the exit
must be someplace special.

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:37.440
Is it?

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:40.150
I thought the same thing.

00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:44.900
Dear Unknown Interview Subject
who is Somewhere in the World,

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:48.360
I want to hear stories from more people.

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:53.650
And so I need to leave this
cramped book-filled... oops.

00:05:54.230 --> 00:05:55.320
You too?

00:05:56.780 --> 00:05:59.230
As I endured the pain from the fall,

00:05:59.230 --> 00:06:03.030
I wrote a poem about the scene I saw as I fell.

00:06:03.030 --> 00:06:05.190
It really is dull here.

00:06:05.190 --> 00:06:08.110
Where is the exit hiding?

00:06:08.110 --> 00:06:09.940
There is no exit.

00:06:09.940 --> 00:06:11.480
There he is again.

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:12.730
Hey, monster cat.

00:06:12.730 --> 00:06:14.230
I'm not a monster cat.

00:06:14.230 --> 00:06:16.690
I'm just a regular cat.

00:06:16.690 --> 00:06:18.610
Normal cats don't talk.

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:21.440
It sighed!

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:23.230
It is a monster cat.

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:25.980
Do monster cats sigh?

00:06:25.980 --> 00:06:27.320
Do you have proof?

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:30.570
No? But they do, obviously. They're monsters.

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:34.730
Listen to what the acting Director says.

00:06:34.730 --> 00:06:40.230
You don't understand your roles
as reincarnated authors at all.

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:42.480
I don't know what that even means.

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:45.530
Hey, I heard your book got tainted!

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:47.030
Loser!

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:49.610
I'm listening, sir, so please continue.

00:06:49.610 --> 00:06:52.280
Shusei, you're a good person.

00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:53.530
Very plain, though.

00:06:53.530 --> 00:06:54.980
Shut up, Shimazaki.

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:59.400
First, there's no exit from the library.

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:03.280
Secondly, even if there was,
you have nowhere to go.

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:04.480
What does that mean?

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:11.690
As I said before, you are souls,
modeled after authors of the past.

00:07:11.690 --> 00:07:17.360
As souls, the only place you can
maintain human form is this space.

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:21.860
Because we're souls,
we can't die while we're here?

00:07:21.860 --> 00:07:27.880
"Run, Melos"

00:07:21.860 --> 00:07:22.900
Yes.

00:07:22.900 --> 00:07:25.400
And because you are souls without bodies,

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:28.070
you can delve into books.

00:07:28.070 --> 00:07:31.690
Wait, did you say "reincarnated" back there?

00:07:31.690 --> 00:07:36.360
The rest of them weren't
saved from books like me?

00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:38.440
No way.

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:42.320
What kind of loser gets stuck in a book?

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:43.820
Then how?

00:07:43.820 --> 00:07:48.360
We were called here directly,
in the form of reincarnation.

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:50.940
Called by who?

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:52.230
That is...

00:07:52.230 --> 00:07:53.940
The Alchemist.

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:55.780
Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> !

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:57.620
"Ryunosuke Akutagawa"

00:07:55.780 --> 00:07:57.570
Morning, everyone.

00:07:58.650 --> 00:08:00.230
It's past noon.

00:08:00.230 --> 00:08:03.610
When I wake up, that's morning for me!

00:08:03.610 --> 00:08:05.320
Amazing, Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> !

00:08:05.320 --> 00:08:07.530
A new interpretation of the word "morning!"

00:08:07.530 --> 00:08:09.480
It's just an excuse for sleeping in late.

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:12.440
Well, if it isn't you-know-who.

00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:15.280
I didn't want to see your face, I don't think.

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:17.900
Today, you're going to tell me...

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:21.530
...what really goes on in the mind
of Ryunosuke Akutagawa.

00:08:21.530 --> 00:08:24.480
I'm not telling you a thing.

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:26.530
How many times do I have to say that?

00:08:26.530 --> 00:08:28.030
Forget it.

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:31.190
What's wrong?

00:08:32.530 --> 00:08:36.530
It seems like I'm not welcome, so I'm going.

00:08:36.530 --> 00:08:40.730
He and I have never gotten along.

00:08:40.730 --> 00:08:42.530
Back to our discussion.

00:08:42.530 --> 00:08:46.280
What reincarnates authors to fight the Taints,

00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:51.400
and creates the library to give
their souls a place to dwell,

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:54.150
is the Alchemist.

00:08:54.150 --> 00:09:00.360
The Alchemist. That's a pretty fancy name.

00:09:00.360 --> 00:09:03.110
What is the Alchemist?

00:09:03.110 --> 00:09:06.190
A being that exists to fight the Taints.

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:08.980
Nothing more can be said.

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:11.650
So what, we don't know?

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:15.940
But even without knowing,
we can still go forward.

00:09:15.940 --> 00:09:18.280
I'll fight the Taints.

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:20.860
For my own sake as well.

00:09:20.860 --> 00:09:22.530
Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> .

00:09:25.230 --> 00:09:26.820
It's strange...

00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:32.150
You can see the stars from here,
but it's not connected to the outside world.

00:09:32.150 --> 00:09:37.940
If anything, it's arrogance to think
that everything you see is connected.

00:09:37.940 --> 00:09:42.320
We have no way of knowing
if those are even real stars.

00:09:42.320 --> 00:09:44.110
Correct.

00:09:44.110 --> 00:09:46.570
They may be fake.

00:09:46.570 --> 00:09:49.110
But they are pretty.

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:50.070
Yes.

00:09:50.070 --> 00:09:56.650
Just because they're fake does not lessen
their shine or beauty, I think.

00:09:56.650 --> 00:10:03.650
If it were otherwise, then nothing
we authors created would have any value.

00:10:03.650 --> 00:10:07.570
You may not be able to reach them.
They may not really exist.

00:10:07.570 --> 00:10:10.030
But still, you can think
of those stars as beautiful.

00:10:10.030 --> 00:10:15.230
I think that ability is what
makes life worth living.

00:10:15.230 --> 00:10:19.900
Is that why you fight to protect the books?

00:10:19.900 --> 00:10:21.360
Yes.

00:10:21.360 --> 00:10:24.230
But that's not all.

00:10:24.230 --> 00:10:28.570
I have no memories of my life as
the author Ryunosuke Akutagawa.

00:10:28.570 --> 00:10:30.150
You don't?

00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:33.530
I hear the titles of the books I wrote,

00:10:33.530 --> 00:10:35.820
but I don't know why I wrote them,

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:38.230
or what I felt when I did.

00:10:38.230 --> 00:10:40.570
I just can't remember.

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:42.480
Why?

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:44.530
I don't know.

00:10:44.530 --> 00:10:47.070
Yes. I don't know.

00:10:47.070 --> 00:10:50.440
And that's why I want to keep going forward.

00:10:50.440 --> 00:10:55.070
If I purify a book and save an author
who knows Ryunosuke Akutagawa well,

00:10:55.070 --> 00:10:58.230
perhaps it will help me remember who I am.

00:10:58.230 --> 00:11:02.360
And that's why you fight!

00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:03.480
Yes.

00:11:03.480 --> 00:11:07.070
I'm trying to find myself, you could say.
It's selfish, huh?

00:11:07.070 --> 00:11:08.150
No...

00:11:08.150 --> 00:11:10.690
I understand how you feel, Dazai- <i>kun</i> .

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:13.110
You're being told to fight
just because you're an author.

00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:16.610
And bossed around by a cat! What the hell?

00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:19.030
That's more than just a simple cat.

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:23.730
It speaks for the Alchemist, you could say.

00:11:23.730 --> 00:11:26.860
But why a cat, you think?

00:11:26.860 --> 00:11:28.070
No idea.

00:11:29.440 --> 00:11:31.320
But there's one thing I do know.

00:11:33.360 --> 00:11:35.070
I'm glad it wasn't a dog.

00:11:41.940 --> 00:11:42.940
What?

00:11:43.690 --> 00:11:46.480
Someone came back from a delve.

00:11:46.480 --> 00:11:49.030
I think it must be...

00:11:53.320 --> 00:11:54.400
Is that...?

00:11:57.690 --> 00:12:01.530
Hey, I know that voice...

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:02.940
You're...

00:12:02.940 --> 00:12:05.110
...Saku Oda!

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:06.620
"Sakunosuke Oda"

00:12:05.110 --> 00:12:07.980
So you're here, too?

00:12:07.980 --> 00:12:11.320
Sorry I couldn't make a cooler introduction...

00:12:12.230 --> 00:12:14.780
Saku Oda! Wake up!

00:12:14.780 --> 00:12:16.150
Saku Oda!

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:24.030
Saku Oda will survive, right?

00:12:24.030 --> 00:12:25.280
We don't know.

00:12:25.280 --> 00:12:26.570
Why?

00:12:26.570 --> 00:12:29.190
You're the one who said that souls don't die!

00:12:29.190 --> 00:12:32.690
Wounds inflicted in a book are different.

00:12:32.690 --> 00:12:37.900
The Taints have the power
to destroy an Author's very soul.

00:12:37.900 --> 00:12:41.570
Thus, wounds received when delving
are carved into the body.

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:44.530
If those wounds are fatal, then...

00:12:44.530 --> 00:12:47.030
They'll die?

00:12:47.030 --> 00:12:51.280
Then why'd you make Saku Oda
go to such a dangerous place himself!

00:12:51.280 --> 00:12:54.320
We didn't want to, damn it!

00:12:54.320 --> 00:12:58.730
Only the authors called by
the tainted book can delve into it.

00:12:58.730 --> 00:13:02.570
This time, that was only Sakunosuke Oda.

00:13:02.570 --> 00:13:04.900
He was probably chosen by the author.

00:13:04.900 --> 00:13:08.780
The book being tainted this time is <i>In the Forest</i>
<i>of the Cherry Blossoms, Beneath the Full Bloom</i> .

00:13:08.780 --> 00:13:11.480
Its author was Ango Sakaguchi.

00:13:11.480 --> 00:13:12.780
Ango!

00:13:14.070 --> 00:13:15.860
Why wasn't it me?

00:13:15.860 --> 00:13:17.860
But what do we do?

00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:21.150
Saku Oda can't delve like this.

00:13:21.150 --> 00:13:22.820
There's no time...

00:13:22.820 --> 00:13:25.360
I'll try.

00:13:25.360 --> 00:13:26.480
Akutagawa- <i>san</i> ?

00:13:26.480 --> 00:13:31.690
He went inside when I was inside <i>Run, Melos</i> .

00:13:31.690 --> 00:13:35.360
I'm the only one who hasn't tried delving.

00:13:35.360 --> 00:13:39.360
Yes. You're the only one who still has a chance.

00:13:39.360 --> 00:13:40.530
I'll go too.

00:13:42.730 --> 00:13:45.400
Ango's trapped in that book, right?

00:13:45.400 --> 00:13:48.360
Then let me go!

00:13:49.690 --> 00:13:51.030
The Reprobrates.

00:13:51.030 --> 00:13:53.320
A collection of authors from the same era,

00:13:53.320 --> 00:13:55.860
which rejected the literature
that had come before them

00:13:55.860 --> 00:13:58.690
and sought to create its antithesis.

00:13:58.690 --> 00:14:03.440
Ango Sakaguchi was one of their
most important members.

00:14:03.440 --> 00:14:06.400
As was Sakunosuke Oda.
And Osamu Dazai.

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:10.150
I refuse to be grouped with others.

00:14:10.150 --> 00:14:13.230
You're a poet. Not an author.

00:14:13.230 --> 00:14:16.610
I guess you couldn't be counted
as part of the group.

00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:20.820
Ango's a good drinking buddy.

00:14:20.820 --> 00:14:22.400
I don't want him to disappear.

00:14:22.400 --> 00:14:24.610
Ango Sakaguchi, huh?

00:14:24.610 --> 00:14:30.280
I've never met him, but...
I agree with your words.

00:14:30.280 --> 00:14:34.570
There is no literature in this world
which can be allowed to disappear.

00:14:34.570 --> 00:14:40.730
When all the pages turn black,
the book will disappear from this world.

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:47.480
It seems I have the right to delve inside.

00:14:47.480 --> 00:14:48.940
Okay, I'll go too!

00:14:50.190 --> 00:14:52.110
There's little time.

00:14:52.110 --> 00:14:55.190
And whoever you're up against,
they defeated Oda.

00:14:55.190 --> 00:14:56.650
Don't screw up.

00:14:56.650 --> 00:14:58.610
Wait for me, Saku Oda!

00:14:58.610 --> 00:15:01.860
I'll save Ango!

00:15:01.860 --> 00:15:04.360
Here we go, Dazai- <i>kun</i> . Focus.

00:15:22.280 --> 00:15:23.480
What?

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:26.980
No, Dazai- <i>kun</i> ! Focus!

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:29.280
Dazai- <i>kun</i> !

00:15:40.400 --> 00:15:44.280
Delving requires intense concentration.

00:15:44.280 --> 00:15:46.650
I should've explained that better.

00:15:47.480 --> 00:15:49.570
Well, it'll work out.

00:16:40.690 --> 00:16:42.900
All I ever do is fall.

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:46.780
But that cherry tree...

00:16:46.780 --> 00:16:48.110
What was that?

00:16:48.690 --> 00:16:49.690
Hello?

00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:52.570
What?

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:53.940
Put those away.

00:16:56.190 --> 00:16:58.280
Forgive our rudeness.

00:16:58.280 --> 00:17:03.070
You fell from the sky and surprised us greatly.

00:17:03.070 --> 00:17:04.530
I see.

00:17:04.530 --> 00:17:05.980
Sorry about that.

00:17:09.690 --> 00:17:11.190
What is it?

00:17:11.190 --> 00:17:14.400
You're pretty.

00:17:19.610 --> 00:17:21.230
Sorry! Sorry!

00:17:23.150 --> 00:17:24.730
You're heading to the capital too?

00:17:24.730 --> 00:17:29.320
Yeah. It's probably the place
with the most people, right?

00:17:29.320 --> 00:17:32.730
I need to go find Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> there.

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:34.360
You're searching for someone?

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:37.110
Yeah. So I'll go with you.

00:17:37.110 --> 00:17:38.690
Okay!

00:17:38.690 --> 00:17:42.530
But why were you lying on the ground there?

00:17:42.530 --> 00:17:45.440
I don't know...

00:17:45.440 --> 00:17:49.190
I saw the cherry blossoms
and suddenly I got scared.

00:17:49.190 --> 00:17:50.940
The cherry blossoms?

00:17:50.940 --> 00:17:52.440
Weird, huh?

00:17:52.440 --> 00:17:54.820
They're so pretty.

00:17:54.820 --> 00:17:57.150
Cherry blossoms are pretty, yes.

00:17:57.150 --> 00:18:02.070
But they're also terrifying, I think.

00:18:02.070 --> 00:18:05.980
This place, Suzuka Pass,
is famous for its cherry trees.

00:18:05.980 --> 00:18:13.030
But when they're in full bloom,
travelers refuse to take this pass.

00:18:13.030 --> 00:18:14.940
Why?

00:18:14.940 --> 00:18:19.610
Because when you travel beneath
the cherry blossoms in full bloom, you go mad.

00:18:20.820 --> 00:18:25.360
So they all run to escape from them.

00:18:26.070 --> 00:18:28.690
Could you have done the same?

00:18:30.610 --> 00:18:33.650
<i>In the Forest of the Cherry Blossoms,</i>
<i>Beneath the Full Bloom</i> .

00:18:33.650 --> 00:18:37.110
If Sakaguchi is trapped by this story's core,

00:18:37.110 --> 00:18:40.530
and the Taints are trying
to change its ending...

00:18:42.320 --> 00:18:44.480
Excuse me. Are you all right?

00:18:45.440 --> 00:18:46.440
Yes.

00:18:48.610 --> 00:18:51.030
I apologize.

00:18:56.190 --> 00:18:59.650
I think this would suit you best.

00:18:59.650 --> 00:19:02.860
Thank you. But it's not for me.

00:19:02.860 --> 00:19:04.480
A present?

00:19:04.480 --> 00:19:05.780
Yes.

00:19:05.780 --> 00:19:10.230
But since you were kind enough
to choose it for me, I'll take this one.

00:19:10.230 --> 00:19:13.110
Thank you. You're a wonderful gentleman.

00:19:13.110 --> 00:19:14.650
You're welcome.

00:19:20.980 --> 00:19:23.280
So this is the capital?

00:19:23.280 --> 00:19:25.730
It's late.

00:19:25.730 --> 00:19:31.320
Dazai- <i>san</i> , stay at my place tonight.

00:19:31.320 --> 00:19:36.570
You seem to know many things I do not.

00:19:36.570 --> 00:19:39.320
I want to hear more from you.

00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:40.480
With pleasure.

00:19:49.860 --> 00:19:52.860
Saku Oda- <i>san</i> ! You need to stay in bed!

00:19:52.860 --> 00:19:56.980
Shusei- <i>san</i> , Dazai- <i>kun</i> left, right?

00:19:56.980 --> 00:20:00.730
Then I need to go...

00:20:00.730 --> 00:20:04.400
You're not up to delving right now!

00:20:04.400 --> 00:20:07.150
Leave it to Akutagawa and Dazai!

00:20:07.150 --> 00:20:09.730
No! Right now, Ango is...

00:20:09.730 --> 00:20:12.730
Right now, Ango is too dangerous!

00:20:16.320 --> 00:20:20.780
If you like, I can teach you
all kinds of things!

00:20:22.980 --> 00:20:24.900
I'm looking forward--

00:20:42.190 --> 00:20:44.360
Is that you...?

00:20:44.360 --> 00:20:46.320
Ango?

00:20:47.230 --> 00:20:48.650
Give it to me.

00:20:48.650 --> 00:20:52.070
Give me your head.

00:21:11.440 --> 00:21:12.820
Stop it, Ango!

00:21:13.570 --> 00:21:15.570
Don't you recognize me?

00:21:16.440 --> 00:21:17.820
Ango!

00:21:54.860 --> 00:21:57.860
"In the Forest of the Cherry Blossoms,
Beneath the Full Bloom"

00:23:28.320 --> 00:23:29.980
Literary Gourmet!

00:23:28.630 --> 00:23:31.880
"Crispy Chicken Wings."

00:23:32.340 --> 00:23:36.470
"Step Step"

00:23:32.530 --> 00:23:35.940
Everybody always makes me do all the work.

00:23:35.940 --> 00:23:39.400
I'm so hungry...

00:23:41.860 --> 00:23:45.320
This is what I wanted!
Nice simple chicken wings!

00:23:45.320 --> 00:23:47.860
Squeeze some lemon on top of it
and add in some rice...

00:23:47.900 --> 00:23:49.610
"Nom nom" "Aah"

00:23:49.610 --> 00:23:53.730
Bean jam bun. For some reason,
I really want that bean jam bun he's eating.

00:23:53.730 --> 00:23:56.360
Bean jam. Bean jam. Gears of Bean Jam!

00:23:56.360 --> 00:23:58.400
Excuse me! Give me a bean jam bun!

00:23:56.410 --> 00:23:58.120
"Nom nom" "Yes!"

00:23:58.400 --> 00:24:00.030
You too, Shusei?
